  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 235.32pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 259.2pt, "This work advances a fundamentally new approach to space-based construction by using liquid ")
  #line-at(72pt, 275.04pt, "self-organization in microgravity as a generative design and fabrication principle. Building on the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 290.88pt, "LiquiFab")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(116.76pt, 290.88pt, " method, we demonstrate how minimal-surface architectures - traditionally dependent on ")
  #line-at(72pt, 306.84pt, "complex additive manufacturing - can instead emerge directly from the physics of fluid interfaces ")
  #line-at(72pt, 322.68pt, "shaped by programmable boundary conditions. We present a simulation-to-fabrication workflow, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 338.52pt, "that includes a boundary-driven minimal-surface solver integrated in Grasshopper/Rhino, and an ")
  #line-at(72pt, 354.36pt, "experimental system that implements in a neutral buoyancy environment simulating microgravity. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 370.32pt, "This enables the generation of customizable Schwarz-P-inspired with tunable geometry and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 386.16pt, "thickness, illustrating a scalable pathway for material-efficient, on-orbit fabrication. To validate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 402pt, "performance in true microgravity, a flight experiment on the International Space Station is ")
  #line-at(72pt, 417.84pt, "scheduled for the first quarter of 2027 and we here detail the additional considerations required for ")
  #line-at(72pt, 433.8pt, "this experiment.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 457.56pt, "Keywords ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 481.44pt, "form-finding, space-oriented design, in-space manufacturing, LiquiFab ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 505.32pt, "INTRODUCTION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 535.2pt, "As human activity in space expands, there is an increasing demand for in-situ and on-demand ")
  #line-at(72pt, 551.04pt, "construction methods capable of operating directly in space (Arney et al., 2021). Recent efforts ")
  #line-at(72pt, 567pt, "have focused on adapting terrestrial manufacturing technologies for use aboard the International ")
  #line-at(72pt, 582.84pt, "Space Station (ISS), including the introduction of in-situ 3D printing in 2014 (Prater & Werkheiser, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 598.68pt, "2018). While additive manufacturing offers geometric flexibility and on-demand production, it ")
  #line-at(72pt, 614.52pt, "remains constrained by the printer’s build envelope and by the requirement for the printer to visit ")
  #line-at(72pt, 630.48pt, "each voxel in space, which limit scalability. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 660.36pt, "A recent technique, LiquiFab (Hochman et al., 2025), demonstrated a new fabrication approach: a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 676.2pt, "volume of liquid polymer is injected into an immiscible immersion liquid matched in density, so ")
  #line-at(72pt, 692.04pt, "that buoyancy precisely cancels gravity and surface tension becomes the sole active force. In this ")
  #line-at(72pt, 707.88pt, "effectively weightless state, a small set of solid boundary surfaces placed in the fluid drives the ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(275.16pt, 752.64pt, "Page ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(302.52pt, 752.64pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(308.88pt, 752.64pt, " of ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324pt, 752.64pt, "13")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.16pt, "liquid away from its natural spherical form and into a new minimum-energy configuration that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 99pt, "conforms to the prescribed constraints. Once the desired shape is reached, UV exposure solidifies ")
  #line-at(72pt, 114.84pt, "the polymer into a solid object.  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 144.72pt, "That work also introduced the concept of \"LiquiBricks\" - modular units assembled sequentially to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 160.68pt, "build up larger constructs. Once a LiquiBrick is solidified, its faces and edges serve as the boundary ")
  #line-at(72pt, 176.52pt, "conditions for the next injection: fresh liquid polymer is introduced, wets the existing solid ")
  #line-at(72pt, 192.36pt, "surfaces, and adopts a new minimum-energy form continuous with the preceding element. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 208.2pt, "Repeating this stepwise process, complex three-dimensional assemblies can be built without a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 224.16pt, "conventional mold or print head. Theoretically, the process is scale-invariant: in the absence of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 240pt, "gravity the LiquiFab approach could be implemented at any size. In practice, however, the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 255.84pt, "achievable brick size in the Earth-based neutral-buoyancy setting is bounded by the precision of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 271.68pt, "density matching, the curing kinetics of the polymer, and the capacity for heat dissipation during ")
  #line-at(72pt, 287.64pt, "the exothermic polymerization reaction. In Space, the first limitation is eliminated, but the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 303.48pt, "remaining two persist.  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 363.24pt, "Building on this foundation, the present study focuses on the design and realization of minimal-")
  #line-at(72pt, 379.08pt, "surface LiquiBricks inspired by the Schwarz-P unit cell, a triply periodic minimal surface (Schoen, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 394.92pt, "1970), presented in Figure 1. Minimal surface lattice structures are widely recognized in aerospace ")
  #line-at(72pt, 410.76pt, "engineering for their high strength-to-weight ratio and efficient material distribution and are ")
  #line-at(72pt, 426.72pt, "therefore ideal candidates for construction of space structures. However, due to their geometric ")
  #line-at(72pt, 442.56pt, "complexity their fabrication typically relies on additive manufacturing. In this work we show that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 458.4pt, "the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(89.4pt, 458.4pt, "LiquiFab")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.16pt, 458.4pt, " approach can readily produce such structures. We introduce a programmable design-")
  #line-at(72pt, 474.24pt, "to-fabrication workflow of customized thin-shelled minimal surface geometries and the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 490.08pt, "development of a semi-automated experimental system operating in a simulated microgravity ")
  #line-at(72pt, 506.04pt, "environment. The experiment objective is to create a physical element within the bounding box ")
  #line-at(72pt, 521.88pt, "with the dimensions of: 80x80x80 mm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(258.84pt, 517.32pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(262.92pt, 521.88pt, ". We design the experimental system such that it could be ")
  #line-at(72pt, 537.72pt, "directly adapted for demonstration on the International Space Station, planned for the first quarter ")
  #line-at(72pt, 553.56pt, "of 2027.  ")
]

